hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"216","It was narrated by Yusuf ibn Musa, it was narrated by Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Saad ibn Ubaidah, he said: Al-Baraa ibn Aazib narrated to me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “When you come to bed, perform your ablution for prayer, then lie on your right side,” then he mentioned the hadith. Abu Bakr said: This word: “If you come to your bed” is from the type that we say the Arabs have, it says: If you do such and such, you mean if You wanted to do that thing, as God Almighty said: O you who have believed, when you stand up for prayer, Surat Al-Ma’idah, verse 6, and what it means is if you want to stand up for prayer. Prayer"
